  "companyName": "NCR Atleos Corporation",
  "country": "US",
  "debtToEquityTTM": null,
  "description": "NCR Atleos Corporation operates as a prominent financial technology firm, specializing in delivering self-service financial solutions. The company serves a diverse global clientele, encompassing financial institutions, merchants, manufacturers, retailers, and individual consumers throughout the United States, the broader Americas, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and the Asia Pacific region. Its business is structured into three primary segments: Self-Service Banking, Network, and Telecommunications & Technology (T&T). Under the Self-Service Banking segment, NCR Atleos provides a full spectrum of automated teller machine (ATM) hardware and software. This is supported by an array of services, including installation, continuous maintenance, and both managed and professional support. Additionally, it offers an \"ATM as a Service\" model, where it comprehensively manages and operates ATMs for financial institutions, covering back-office functions, cash management, software administration, and unit deployment. The Network segment features an extensive infrastructure of ATMs and versatile financial services kiosks, catering to financial institutions, fintech companies, neobanks, and retailers. A significant offering is the Allpoint network, which enables cash withdrawal and deposit access for a broad range of providers, such as credit unions, banks, digital banks, fintechs, and issuers of stored-value debit cards. This segment also encompasses ATM branding services, complete ATM management for retailers and other businesses, and the LibertyX solution, which empowers consumers to buy and sell Bitcoin. Lastly, the Telecommunications & Technology (T&T) segment focuses on providing managed network and infrastructure services to enterprise clients across various sectors. These services are often delivered in collaboration with communications service providers and technology manufacturers. It also extends professional, on-site, and remote support for advanced network technologies, including software-defined wide area networking (SD-WAN), network functions virtualization (NFV), wireless local area networks (WLAN), optical networking, and edge networks. NCR Atleos Corporation was founded in 1884 and its corporate headquarters are located in Atlanta, Georgia.",
